--
Construction vtables (Itanium C++ ABI 2.6.2) for the direct bases with
virtual bases of a complete object: `virtual_table::X@B@D' holds B's
overriders with D's virtual-base offsets, installed in B's subobject
pointers (including the shared virtual base's) around B's base-object
constructor and destructor, so a virtual call from B's constructor -- also
through a V* -- reaches B's overrider (N5008 [class.cdtor]/4).  Only the
complete object installs them (it alone knows the offsets); a base-object
constructor of a class that is itself a base leaves the tables its caller
installed -- the documented approximation for deeper levels (the ABI passes
a VTT).
